    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance that is visible from both directions on the road.\n• Keep the driveway clear of parked vehicles to allow fire apparatus to reach the residence.\n• Install a reflective marker or sign identifying the detached structure to help responders locate it quickly on arrival.\n• Trim vegetation along the access drive to maintain clearance for emergency vehicles on both sides and overhead.\n• Clear a turnaround area near the residence or detached structure large enough for emergency vehicles to reverse direction without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Cut back dense vegetation that directly contacts or overhangs the main residence and detached structure.\n• Keep a gate or opening in the perimeter fencing accessible from the front to allow responders to reach the rear of the property on foot.\n• If a rear gate exists, keep it unlocked or secured with a lock compatible with a standard responder key.\n• Mark any pedestrian access points through the perimeter fencing so responders can locate them quickly."
