    "recommendations": "• Trim branches from trees along the driveway that hang over or close to the travel surface to keep the route clear for vehicles.\n\n• Thin the tree cluster nearest the structure to create open space between the trees and the building.\n\n• Remove or cut back shrubs and low plants that are directly against or touching the structure.\n\n• Separate ground vegetation from the base of the structure by clearing a bare or low-grass band around the building.\n\n• Trim low branches on large trees near the structure so flames cannot climb from ground vegetation up into the tree canopy.\n\n• Thin scattered shrubs and mixed vegetation between the tree clusters and the structure to reduce the amount of connected plant material leading toward the building.\n\n• Keep ground vegetation mowed short in open areas between the structure and surrounding trees and shrubs."
